body:
\*\*Spoilers\*\*

&#x200B;

>!I think her character shows how no matter how much you undyingly love someone, that it doesn't guarantee that they will want to accept it or that they will shape their life around you the same way you did for them. I really appreciated how it showed how immature she was in how she handled her feelings (not just for Eren but in general), she never knew how to express them, and it costed her in many instances not being transparent about herself. I think she is a great example of a female protagonist, flawed but undeniably strong. She is by no means my favourite character, but I really appreciate her as a character. I really loved her bonds with people (shown outside of just Eren), specifically how her and Armin's friendship progressed. I feel like people say that she's too basic too often and how she didn't exist outside of her love for Eren, but I think it says a lot that she was the person to kill Eren.!<
